            "generic": "Not quite. Find the quadrant first.",
            "byKey": {
              "arctan": "You used $\\arctan(b/a) = \\arctan(-1)$. That points into the fourth quadrant; $-2 + 2i$ is in the second.",
              "degrees": "That is the angle in degrees. Give it in radians: $135° = 3\\pi/4$."
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "text": "$-2 + 2i$ is up and to the left, halfway between $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\pi$. So $\\operatorname{Arg} z = \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\approx 2.3562$."
          }
        }
