        "generic": "Not quite. Write each root with $i$ first."
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "$\\sqrt{-2} = i\\sqrt2$ and $\\sqrt{-8} = i\\sqrt8$, so the product is $i^2\\sqrt{16} = -4$. The rule $\\sqrt a\\sqrt b = \\sqrt{ab}$ fails when both are negative."
      }
    },
